---
export const title = 'Accessibility';
export const order = 300;
---

<p>
  Each item renders a real <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code> with one <code>&lt;dt&gt;</code> (the label) and
  one <code>&lt;dd&gt;</code> (the slotted value and actions). A <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code> cannot wrap
  slotted children across a shadow root, so every pair is its own list, and screen readers pair each
  label with its value. An empty value is a dash hidden from screen readers, with "Not set" read in
  its place.
</p>
<p>
  The string is translated with <code>setPeacockStrings()</code>: <code>notSet</code>.
</p>
